# clipsdaily — standing rules

This checkout is the clipsdaily pipeline (record live streams, cut vertical clips, post to YouTube Shorts / TikTok / Instagram Reels, submit to clipping campaigns).

## Never break these

- **Full frame, no cropping.** Every clip shows the whole 16:9 source frame on a 1080x1920 canvas, blurred darkened copy behind it.
- **One-line post captions, no boilerplate, no hashtags** except ones a campaign requires (`#IShowSpeed`).
- **No burned-in word captions.** One big hook overlay at the start only (~3s), hook at y=300.
- **Strict eligibility gate.** `eligibility_gate.py` must PASS before any campaign clip posts or submits. Borderline = blocked.
- **Never submit a clip twice, or past 30 minutes after posting.**
- **Credit the streamer** in every post.
- **Clipsdaily accounts only.** Never point this at a personal account.
- **TikTok auto-posting is blocked** (throttled session + Playwright sync/async bug). Do not retry repeatedly; retries deepen the throttle.

## Commands

```bash
clipsdaily run            # live runner
clipsdaily post now       # post next pending clip
clipsdaily queue status   # queue health
clipsdaily campaign watch --check
clipsdaily submit scan
clipsdaily earnings
```

## Repo vs live

This repo is the dev copy. The live runtime is `/home/abel/clipsdaily` on indra. Never edit the live dir by hand; deploy with `bash deploy.sh`. Never run `restart_maintainer.py` (it wipes `queue.json`).
